 "answer": {
  "answer": "At 2 Hz planning the study confirmed only one of the five challenging settings it was looking for, so the goal was not met. The confirmed setting is on scene 09a95ffa, with the cars shifted 1.5 s earlier at recorded speed (1.0x). Every repeat there failed, but its range only just clears one half. One of those failures was a car cutting in from the ego's rear quarter, which was not the policy's fault. The other two were the policy drifting left into a car passing in the next lane. No other scene failed at any setting tried. At most settings there was only one run, so a pass there is a hint, not evidence that the setting is safe. The study can't say whether the other eight scenes have no failing timing or the search just didn't find one.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "The one confirmed challenging setting is scene 09a95ffa with the cars 1.5 s earlier at 1.0x speed. Every repeat failed, and the failure rate is surely above one half.",
    "settings": [
